<h1>Basic Configuration Parameters group</h1>
<p>The <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/">Folder Parameter test</a> we just
  built doesn't stand on its own - it's one of several tests bundled together under a <strong>test group</strong>
  called <strong>Basic Configuration Parameters</strong>, each demonstrating a different configuration field type.
  You've already seen this group in the execution tree:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/folder-parameter-test-gui.png", "Basic Configuration Parameters test group expanded in the Orcraft controller's Test Explorer, showing all its parameter tests", "large") }}
<p>Let's review the code of the file that defines this group:</p>
{{ cmd.copyPath("orcraft-test-suite-tutorial/test_group_basic_configuration_parameters/") }}

<h2 id="group-file-structure">Group file structure</h2>

<h3 id="imports">Imports</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('from __future__ import annotations

from orcraft import (
	OrcraftTestGroup,
	OrcraftTestGroupConfig,
	OrcraftTestGroupResult,
	OrcraftConfigField,
)

from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_folder_parameter.test_folder_parameter import TestFolderParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_boolean_parameter.test_boolean_parameter import TestBooleanParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_selector_parameter.test_selector_parameter import TestSelectorParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_folder_list_parameter.test_folder_list_parameter import TestFolderListParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_file_parameter.test_file_parameter import TestFileParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_file_list_parameter.test_file_list_parameter import TestFileListParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_numeric_parameter.test_numeric_parameter import TestNumericParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_multi_selector_parameter.test_multi_selector_parameter import TestMultiSelectorParameter
from test_group_basic_configuration_parameters.test_string_parameter.test_string_parameter import TestStringParameter') }}
<p>Unlike a test, a group imports <code>OrcraftTestGroup</code> and <code>OrcraftTestGroupConfig</code> instead of
  <code>OrcraftTest</code> and <code>OrcraftTestConfig</code> - plus one import per test it bundles together.</p>

<h3 id="config-class">Config class</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersConfig(OrcraftTestGroupConfig):
	name = OrcraftConfigField.Text(default="Basic Configuration Parameters")
	description = OrcraftConfigField.Text(
		default="Covers tests that demonstrate configuration parameters used with the maze app."
	)
	tests = OrcraftConfigField.Tests(
		default_factory=lambda: [
			TestFolderParameter(),
			TestBooleanParameter(),
			TestSelectorParameter(),
			TestFolderListParameter(),
			TestFileParameter(),
			TestFileListParameter(),
			TestNumericParameter(),
			TestMultiSelectorParameter(),
			TestStringParameter(),
		]
	)') }}
<p>Just like <code>name</code> and <code>description</code> on a test config, a group config has the same two
  fields - shown for the group itself in the execution tree. The field that matters here is <code>tests</code>,
  declared with <code>OrcraftConfigField.Tests</code>: it's a list of test instances, each one becoming a child
  node of this group in the execution tree, in the order given.</p>
<p>If you want to remove a test from showing up - and running - under this group, you can just comment out its
  line in this list, instead of deleting it.</p>

<h3 id="group-class">Group class</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult(OrcraftTestGroupResult):
	pass


class TestGroupBasicConfigurationParameters(OrcraftTestGroup):
	def __init__(self) -> None:
		super().__init__(config=TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersConfig())
		self.result = TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult()') }}
<p>Unlike a test, a group has no <code>_run_case</code> to implement - running it simply means running every test
  it contains. <code>TestGroupBasicConfigurationParametersResult</code> is empty here, since this group doesn't
  add any result fields of its own beyond what <code>OrcraftTestGroupResult</code> already provides.</p>

<h3 id="main">Main</h3>
{{ codeblock.block('def main() -> None:
	group = TestGroupBasicConfigurationParameters()
	group.run()


if __name__ == "__main__":
	main()') }}
<p>Running the group's <code>main</code> runs every test it contains, one after another, the same way the
  controller does when you run the group node itself.</p>

<h2 id="basic-configuration-parameters">Basic configuration parameters</h2>
<p>Here's a short summary of each test in this group and the parameter type it demonstrates. See the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/">Framework</a> chapter for complete implementation details of each
  field type.</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Test</th>
      <th>Field type</th>
      <th>What it demonstrates</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/">Folder Parameter</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Folder</code></td>
      <td>A single folder path, picked through a folder browser.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Boolean Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Boolean</code></td>
      <td>An on/off toggle, shown as a checkbox.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Selector Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Select</code></td>
      <td>A single choice out of a predefined list of options.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Folder List Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.FolderList</code></td>
      <td>Several folder paths at once, held as a list.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>File Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.File</code></td>
      <td>A single file path, picked through a file browser.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>File List Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.FileList</code></td>
      <td>Several file paths at once, held as a list.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Numeric Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Numeric</code></td>
      <td>A number, optionally bounded by a minimum and maximum.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Multi-Selector Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.MultiSelect</code></td>
      <td>Any number of choices out of a predefined list of options.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>String Parameter</td>
      <td><code>OrcraftConfigField.Text</code></td>
      <td>Free-form text, typed directly into the field.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="folder-parameter">Folder Parameter</h3>
<p>Covered in detail in the two previous chapters -
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/adding-configuration-parameter/">Adding configuration parameter</a> and
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/running-folder-parameter-test/">Running Folder Parameter test</a>. The
  test declares a single <code>Maze Executable Folder</code> field and runs the executable found in it.</p>

<h3 id="boolean-parameter">Boolean Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds a <code>Use --help Switch</code> toggle next to the folder field. When it's on, the maze app is run with
  the <code>--help</code> switch; when off, it's run without it.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/boolean-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the Boolean Parameter test, showing the Use --help Switch checkbox", "large") }}

<h3 id="selector-parameter">Selector Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds a <code>Command</code> field offering the maze app's commands - <code>generate</code>,
  <code>solve</code> and <code>save</code> - as a drop-down, and runs the one selected.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/selector-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the Selector Parameter test with the Command drop-down open, showing Generate, Solve and Save", "large") }}

<h3 id="folder-list-parameter">Folder List Parameter</h3>
<p>Replaces the single folder field with a <code>Maze Executable Folders</code> list, so several version folders
  can be selected at once. The test loops over them, running the selected command against each maze app version
  in turn.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/folder-list-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the Folder List Parameter test, showing the v1.0.0, v2.0.0 and v3.0.0 maze folders selected", "large") }}

<h3 id="file-parameter">File Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds a required <code>Maze Save/Load File</code> field, used as the target of the <code>save</code>,
  <code>load</code> and <code>solve</code> commands - this is where the
  <a class="text-accent" href="/tutorial/maze-application/#generating-maze-save-files">maze save files</a> we
  generated earlier come in.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/file-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the File Parameter test, showing the Maze Save/Load File field set to a saved maze JSON file", "large") }}

<h3 id="file-list-parameter">File List Parameter</h3>
<p>Takes a <code>Maze Save/Load Files</code> list instead of a single file, running the selected command once per
  file - for example solving <code>maze.json</code>, <code>maze2.json</code> and <code>maze3.json</code> in one
  test.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/file-list-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the File List Parameter test, showing maze.json, maze2.json and maze3.json listed in the Maze Save/Load Files field", "large") }}

<h3 id="numeric-parameter">Numeric Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds several numeric fields - <code>Width</code>, <code>Height</code>, <code>Seed</code> and the
  <code>Start</code>/<code>End</code> coordinates - which are passed to the maze app as its generation options.
  This test also shows how fields are arranged into rows in the configuration panel.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/numeric-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the Numeric Parameter test, showing the Width, Height, Seed and Start/End coordinate fields", "large") }}

<h3 id="multi-selector-parameter">Multi-Selector Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds an <code>Algorithms</code> field where any combination of <code>BFS</code>, <code>DFS</code> and
  <code>ASTAR</code> can be selected, alongside <code>Solve Switches</code> and <code>Generation Switches</code>
  fields that pick which switches are passed to the maze app. The test runs it once per selected algorithm.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/multi-selector-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the Multi-Selector Parameter test, showing the Solve Switches, Algorithms and Generation Switches multi-select fields", "large") }}

<h3 id="string-parameter">String Parameter</h3>
<p>Adds a free-text <code>Command Line</code> field holding a raw argument string, together with a
  <code>Use String Command Line</code> toggle that decides whether that string is passed through as-is or the
  arguments are built from the other fields.</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/tutorial/basic-configuration-parameters-group/string-parameter.png", "Configuration panel of the String Parameter test, showing the Use String Command Line toggle and the raw Command Line text field", "large") }}
